                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "The OpenBMC motto is send it upstream and then ask Joel to pull your changes into our OpenBMC fork at git://github.com/openbmc/linux until the changes land in upstream (and then Joel just picks the official changes up in a rebase). \n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/kernel-development.md is a little old but the general idea is the same. You'd want to send your patches out on the OpenBMC mailing list and ask Joel to pick them up in the OpenBMC Linux fork."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "To be absolutely clear, pointing at another fork of the kernel is not acceptable.  There are multiple aspects of the meta-layer guidelines which this would be breaking.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/meta-layer-guidelines.md"
                }
